 "limitations": [
  "Labels are produced by an AI annotator (Claude) following the project's labelling guide, not by humans; gold v1 and gold v2 are annotated by the same family, so shared bias is possible and is not measured: a model that imitates the annotator's conventions would look better than it is. Gold v2 has two independent blind passes (agreement and kappa in data/gold_v2/agreement.json) which bound noise, not shared bias. Human adjudication of the queued rows is still outstanding.",
  "Chosen by a pre-registered rule from a fixed list of designs on pooled held-out sets, but after a dry run on gold v1 and the replay check had shown a large early-fusion gain. Two guards were added afterwards and only make adoption harder: evaluation rows within cosine 0.90 of a training text (e5-large) are removed, and the gain must hold on what remains; and a cost rule picks the cheapest candidate within 0.02 of the best. Both are disclosed in configs/evidence_v2.yaml and docs/EVIDENCE_V2.md.",
  "It needs a sentence encoder (intfloat/multilingual-e5-large, 560M parameters, about 105 ms per text on CPU at batch 32, 2.7 GB resident) for any text that is not in the pinned replay embeddings. The frozen replay pack is covered by hash-pinned float16 vectors so the default run needs no torch; a new document needs `pip install -r requirements-embed.txt`.",
  "Dev rows select the hyper-parameters, fit the temperature and decide which classes are flagged unreliable: scores on dev are optimistic.",
  "No untouched evaluation set remains for this model. Gold v1, gold v2 and the replay check all fed the pooled statistic that adopted it (and gold v1 and the replay check were read by the dry run), so the acceptance bar below, although met, is not independent evidence. The choice was among five fixed designs with a large effect on every set separately, but an independent check needs new labels: the human adjudication queue (data/gold_v2/adjudication_v2.csv) and a fresh sample.",
  "Roughly 3,000 annotated rows. Rare classes have few examples: see the per-class reliability table. A class flagged unreliable is never asserted; its documents are shown as UNCERTAIN.",
  "Event type is judged from the headline or tweet alone (no article body, no price data). Multi-event texts get the dominant event only.",
  "Probability calibration was fitted on dev rows; on other sources probabilities can be over-confident (see ECE per evaluation set).",
  "The impact models (impact-v1 and impact-v2) were trained on the TF-IDF event model's probabilities, so the impact stage keeps reading those (train/serve parity); only the user-facing event stage uses this model."
 ]
}
